{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QmAaq2h9sjoe9GdsERhi85","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — struct_self_consist_ie\n2\t\n3\t> Updated 2026-05-15 — D070 REFRAMING: from \"gap finding\" to \"regime-specific bottleneck identification with controlled ablation\". Motivated by 6-round 3.0/5 plateau — Reviewer diagnosis: content ceiling, not framing ceiling. Adding free-form decoding ablation as breakthrough experiment.\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR May 2026)\n7\t- Deadline: ARR May cycle, 2026-05-25\n8\t\n9\t## Core Claims (3 条, D070 重排)\n10\t\n11\t### Claim 1 (PRIMARY — Regime-Specific Selection Bottleneck)\n12\tThe correlation-selection gap in structured IE is **caused by constrained decoding**. Under constrained decoding (Outlines/grammar-guided), logprob score compression makes per-sample ranking impossible: 60% of instances have within-sample logprob range < 0.05. Controlled ablation via free-form generation confirms the mechanism: removing constrained decoding recovers logprob variance and selection ability.\n13\t\n14\t**Two-layer argument**:\n15\t- Layer 1 (definitional, noted not discovered): 4/5 signals are instance-level aggregates → cannot rank candidates by construction. This is a conceptual clarification of QE vs selection conflation in prior work, not an empirical finding.\n16\t- Layer 2 (empirical, the core contribution): (a) Logprob — the only per-sample signal — fails due to score compression under constrained decoding. (b) Consensus-proximity/MBR strategies also fail despite success in MT (non-trivial). (c) **Free-form ablation**: removing constrained decoding recovers logprob discrimination → proves compression is the bottleneck, not an inherent IE limitation.\n17\t\n18\t**Key evidence (constrained)**:\n19\t- Non-tied subset (40%): logprob selection +2.9pp vs greedy (p=0.01), within-instance ρ: 0.08→0.39\n20\t- Full set: logprob +0.6pp, bootstrap p=0.39, Cohen's d=0.038 (negligible), 95% CI [-3.0, +4.2]pp\n21\t- Oracle headroom: NER +13pp, RE +18pp → information exists but signals can't access it under constrained decoding\n22\t\n23\t**Key evidence (free-form ablation)** [PLANNED — exp_freeform_ablation]:\n24\t- Hypothesis: Free-form generation on SciERC will show (a) wider logprob variance, (b) improved logprob selection performance\n25\t- If confirmed: gap is regime-specific → constrained decoding is the bottleneck\n26\t- If not: gap is inherent to structured IE → stronger universal finding\n27\t\n28\t**Implications**: Not just \"signals don't work\" but \"here's WHY and WHEN they don't work, and here's a path forward\" (relaxed decoding + post-hoc filtering, or use logprob on non-tied subset).\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 2 (METHODOLOGY — QE Evaluation Framework)\n31\tSystematic evaluation of 5 confidence signals across 4 families for structured IE quality estimation. This is the methodological infrastructure, not a primary contribution.\n32\t\n33\t**Key results**:\n34\t- NER: EM AUROC 0.749, voting_conf ρ=0.379, SJ ρ=0.360 — all >> logprob (AUROC 0.578, ρ=0.205)\n35\t- RE (preliminary, single benchmark): voting_conf leads both full and conditional\n36\t- Difficulty-dependent signal ranking: WNUT-17 conditional collapse (ρ significant → n.s.) + logprob ρ=−0.410 (non-obvious: overconfidence on OOD)\n37\t- Temperature robustness: SJ Δρ=±0.01 vs FK Δρ=±0.06-0.09\n38\t\n39\t**Evidence preserved from original Claim 1** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0, exp_012_rerun_1024):\n40\t- NER full (n=529): ρ — voting_conf 0.379, SJ 0.360, EM 0.295, FK 0.267, logprob 0.205; AUROC — EM 0.749, SJ 0.692, voting_conf 0.684, FK 0.629, logprob 0.578\n41\t- RE full (n=397): AUROC — EM 0.706, voting_conf 0.694, SJ 0.670, FK 0.609, logprob 0.601\n42\t- ECE (NER): EM 0.353, voting 0.381, SJ 0.453, FK 0.451, logprob 0.706\n43\t\n44\t### Claim 2b (Selection evidence)\n45\t**exp_016_rerun_1024 evidence** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0):\n46\t- NER best-of-N (n=529): logprob 0.6501 > sj 0.6450 = ensemble 0.6450 > greedy 0.6439 > voting 0.6337 > random 0.6077 (oracle 0.7758)\n47\t- RE best-of-N (n=397): greedy 0.4042 > logprob 0.3948 > sj 0.3855 = ensemble 0.3855 > voting 0.3592 > random 0.3544 (oracle 0.5850)\n48\t\n49\t**exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap evidence** (3-seed bootstrap, 1000 iterations):\n50\t- NER logprob vs greedy: bootstrap 95% CI [−0.030, +0.042], permutation p=0.39\n51\t- Effect size: Cohen's d=0.038 (negligible), sign test win rate=0.466\n52\t\n53\t### Claim 3 (Diagnostic — task-complexity boundary)\n54\tThe effectiveness of consistency-based confidence is governed by task structural complexity: compound error propagation in relational tasks degrades the consistency-accuracy correlation on the full instance set, but the signal remains valid within the model's capability range. This boundary applies across all confidence signals tested.\n55\t\n56\t**MVP evidence**: RE full vs cond AUROC lift — EM: 0.706→0.752 (+4.6pp), SJ: 0.670→0.646 (−2.4pp, 待确认), voting_conf: 0.694→0.642 (−5.2pp, 待确认). Component decomposition shows all RE components equally weak (head_sj rho=0.210). T=0.7 naturally separates knowledge-gap vs uncertainty errors.\n57\t\n58\t**exp-005 evidence**: Conditional filtering dwarfs temperature tuning — RE SJ cond lift +0.07~0.14 vs temperature effect ±0.01. T=1.0 preserves more oracle headroom (RE: 0.167 vs 0.131) and diversity (1-SJ: 0.389 vs 0.313). Recommendation: T=1.0 + conditional filtering, not temperature optimization.\n59\t\n60\t**exp-001 N-scaling evidence** (SciERC, n=200 subset, ⚠️ needs full-set confirmation):\n61\t- RE N=16: voting_conf ρ=0.448 (vs N=8 0.340, +0.108), SJ ρ=0.333 (vs 0.244, +0.089), all signals improve +0.07~0.10\n62\t- NER N=16: flat (already saturated at N=8) — voting_conf 0.401 vs 0.392\n63\t- **Key insight**: The task-complexity boundary is partially a SAMPLE BUDGET boundary. Compound error propagation increases per-instance variance, requiring more samples (N=16 vs N=8) to average out noise. This makes Claim 2 more nuanced: RE consistency fails at N=8 not because the signal is absent, but because it's noisier and needs more samples to manifest.\n64\t- ⚠️ Caveat: exp-001 ran on 200/529 instances. Full-set replication needed before claiming in paper.\n65\t\n66\t## Story Spine (D070 REFRAMED)\n67\t\n68\t**Problem**: Test-time scaling via multi-sample generation improves LLM reasoning, but its effectiveness for structured information extraction is unclear. Practitioners need to know: can confidence signals select better outputs from multiple candidates?\n69\t\n70\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-consistency (Wang et al. 2023) succeeds for discrete-answer reasoning. MBR decoding succeeds for MT. But structured IE outputs (entity sets, relation triples) under constrained decoding present a fundamentally different challenge — and prior work conflates quality estimation with selection.\n71\t\n72\t**Our framing (D070 reposition — from \"finding a gap\" to \"identifying and verifying a bottleneck\")**:\n73\t\n74\tWe systematically compare five confidence signals for IE under constrained decoding, and discover a **regime-specific selection bottleneck**:\n75\t1. **Conceptual clarification**: Four of five signals are instance-level by construction and cannot rank candidates — this is noted as a definitional property, not discovered empirically. The interesting question is whether the remaining strategies (logprob, MBR/consensus-proximity) can select.\n76\t2. **Core empirical finding**: Logprob — the only per-sample signal — fails due to score compression under constrained decoding (60% of instances have within-sample range < 0.05). Consensus-proximity/MBR also fails despite success in MT.\n77\t3. **Controlled verification**: Free-form decoding ablation confirms the mechanism — removing constrained decoding recovers logprob's discriminative power. The gap is regime-specific, not inherent to structured IE.\n78\t4. **Practical pathway**: Non-tied instances (+2.9pp, p=0.01) show logprob works when compression is absent → actionable mitigation via relaxed decoding or non-tied subset selection.\n79\t\n80\t**Headline**: \"We identify, diagnose, and experimentally verify a regime-specific selection bottleneck in constrained-decoding IE: confidence signals that reliably predict output quality (AUROC 0.75) cannot select better candidates because constrained decoding compresses log-probability scores. A controlled free-form ablation confirms the mechanism and points to relaxed decoding as a mitigation path.\"\n81\t\n82\t**Potential title**: \"The Constrained Decoding Bottleneck: Why Confidence Signals Predict but Cannot Select in Information Extraction\"\n83\t\n84\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n85\t\n86\t### R1: \"Only one NER dataset — generalization unclear\"\n87\t- **Mitigation**: 2 datasets (SciERC + CoNLL-2003) × 2 models (Qwen3 + LLaMA) = 4 NER configurations. exp_017_llama_conll_infer SJ ρ=0.431 matches Qwen CoNLL ρ=0.436, demonstrating cross-model × cross-dataset consistency. Limitation: informal text domains (social media etc.) not covered — acknowledge in Limitations section.\n88\t- **Priority**: P0\n89\t\n90\t### R2: \"Only one model family (Qwen3-8B)\"\n91\t- **Mitigation**: exp-007 (LLaMA-3.1-8B) shows model-agnostic effect\n92\t- **Priority**: P0\n93\t\n94\t### R3: \"FK is a strawman baseline — what about log-prob, USC, exact-match?\"\n95\t- **Mitigation**: exp-012 (log-prob), exp-013 (exact-match), exp-014 (entity voting) provide comprehensive baseline comparison. Results: structural consistency family (EM+SJ+voting) >> log-prob >> FK. USC discussed in related work (LLM-as-judge, orthogonal approach).\n96\t- **Priority**: P0, RESOLVED — results decisive\n97\t\n98\t### R3b: \"EM beats voting_conf and SJ on AUROC — why present SJ/voting_conf?\"\n99\t- **Mitigation**: EM is a strict binary signal (all-or-nothing match); SJ captures partial agreement and generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs (relations, events). Voting_conf provides granular entity-level scores. NER full AUROC: EM 0.749 > SJ 0.692 > voting_conf 0.684, but ρ: voting_conf 0.379 > SJ 0.360 > EM 0.295. EM excels at binary discrimination but underperforms on rank ordering. SJ is also more temperature-robust (Δρ=±0.01). Paper presents all three as complementary instantiations of the structural consistency principle: EM for go/no-go filtering, voting_conf for ranking, SJ for generalizability.\n100\t- **Priority**: P1 — narrative adjusted for 1024-token results\n101\t\n102\t### R4: \"No actual TTS improvement demonstrated\"\n103\t- **Status**: ✅ CONFIRMED by exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap. No signal significantly outperforms greedy on either task. NER logprob +0.6pp not significant (bootstrap p=0.39, 95% CI [−0.030, +0.042], Cohen's d=0.038). RE: greedy > all signals.\n104\t- **Mitigation**: Paper PIVOTS to \"confidence estimation + correlation-selection gap analysis.\" exp-006 redesigned as diagnostic: show selection curves to visualize the gap (F1 vs N per signal + oracle ceiling). The gap itself is a contribution, not a failure.\n105\t- **Priority**: P0 — narrative pivot complete, bootstrap confirms\n106\t\n107\t### R5: \"Sample size N=8 may be too small for reliable SJ estimation\"\n108\t- **Mitigation**: exp-001 (N=16) with multi-seed robustness\n109\t- **Priority**: P0\n110\t\n111\t### R6: \"Conditional analysis cherry-picks favorable instances\"\n112\t- **Mitigation**: Principled separation (knowledge-gap vs uncertainty). Add threshold sensitivity analysis. Temperature analysis provides independent validation.\n113\t- **Priority**: P0 (add sensitivity analysis)\n114\t\n115\t### R7: \"Only ρ as evaluation metric\"\n116\t- **Mitigation**: Add AUROC, calibration plots (ECE), Kendall's τ for all experiments. ECE data now available: NER best calibrated = EM (0.353), RE best = voting (0.272). Logprob worst calibrated (NER 0.706, RE 0.769).\n117\t- **Priority**: P0\n118\t\n119\t### R8: \"Formula-implementation discrepancy\"\n120\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must describe actual algorithm (type-grouped Hungarian matching with max(|g_a|,|g_b|) denominator)\n121\t- **Priority**: P0, paper writing fix\n122\t\n123\t### R9: \"Evaluation circularity (T>0 consistency vs T=0 F1)\"\n124\t- **Mitigation**: Add leave-one-out SJ evaluation as robustness check. Justify cross-mode design (greedy = deterministic reference, standard in TTS literature).\n125\t- **Priority**: P0\n126\t\n127\t### R10: \"Insufficient related work\" (三档一致 [B][M][W])\n128\t- **Mitigation**: Expand to 35+ references. Must cite:\n129\t  - USC (Chen 2024) — empirical differentiation, not just citation\n130\t  - Semantic uncertainty (Kuhn 2023), calibration (Kadavath 2022, Guo 2017, Desai & Durrett 2020)\n131\t  - **Conformal prediction for structured outputs**: Fisch et al. 2021, Angelopoulos et al. 2021, Bates et al. 2021\n132\t  - **Token-level NER uncertainty**: Xiao & Wang 2019, Shelmanov et al. 2021, He et al. 2020\n133\t  - **Ensemble/MC-dropout**: Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017, Gal & Ghahramani 2016\n134\t  - **Verifier/reward models**: Cobbe et al. 2021, Lightman et al. 2023\n135\t  - **TTS scaling theory**: Snell et al. 2024, Brown et al. 2024\n136\t  - **Structured calibration**: Kuleshov & Liang 2015, Jagannatha & Yu 2022\n137\t  - **IE confidence**: Culotta & McCallum 2004\n138\t  - SelfCheckGPT (Manakul 2023), selective prediction (Geifman & El-Yaniv 2017)\n139\t  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 必引]**:\n140\t    - CISC (ACL Findings 2025) — confidence-weighted majority vote for reasoning; 对比：我们用 structural similarity 而非 confidence 加权，且面向 set-structured IE 输出\n141\t    - Self-Certainty Best-of-N (ICLR 2026, arxiv 2502.18581) — KL-divergence reward-free selection; 对比：我们发现 log-prob 是唯一有效 selection signal (与其方向互补)，且揭示 correlation-selection gap\n142\t    - ReASC (2026, arxiv 2601.02970) — reliability-aware adaptive self-consistency; 对比：仍限于 reasoning 离散答案\n143\t    - Atomic Self-Consistency (EMNLP 2024) — 子声明级一致性 for long-form text; 对比：我们在 entity-set 级别做结构化度量\n144\t    - **Nédellec & Xia (Genomics Informatics, 2026-02, PMC12888769)** — \"Consistency–accuracy correlation in hard-prompted LLMs for entity and relation extraction\"。最直接竞争者：4 LLMs 在植物健康 NER/RE 上研究 consistency-accuracy 相关性。**关键差异**：(a) 他们用 surface-level string matching，自承\"overlooks semantically consistent outputs\"，我们的 SJ 正好解决此问题; (b) 不研究 best-of-N selection; (c) 单领域 hard-prompted (T=0); (d) 无多信号家族对比。论文 Intro 可引用其 limitation 作为 SJ 的动机\n145\t  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 应引]**:\n146\t    - UQ for LLMs Survey (ACL Findings 2025) — 最全面 LLM 不确定性综述\n147\t    - UQ+Calibration Survey (arxiv 2503.15850, 2025) — 第二篇综合综述\n148\t    - Semantic Entropy Probes (2024) — 低成本不确定性估计\n149\t    - Latent Self-Consistency (2025, arxiv 2508.18395) — embedding 空间一致性\n150\t    - Ranked Voting SC (2025, arxiv 2505.10772) — 排名投票变体，仍限于推理任务\n151\t    - Know Your Limits: Abstention Survey (TACL 2025) — 选择性预测综述，与 Claim 1 selective prediction 角度直接相关\n152\t    - Confidence Estimation Survey (NAACL 2024, arxiv 2311.08298) — LLM 置信度估计全景定位\n153\t    - **CoCoA (Vashurin et al., NeurIPS 2025, arxiv 2502.04964)** — MBR 框架融合 confidence+consistency 做 UQ，在 QA/摘要/翻译上评估。与我们 exp-016 ensemble (SJ+logprob) 对标，但未涉及 structured IE\n154\t    - **Vashurin et al. (arxiv 2510.20460, 2025)** — VCE/MSP/Sample Consistency/CoCoA 四方法系统评估，任务不含 structured IE\n155\t  - **需新增 Related Work 小节**:\n156\t    - \"Test-Time Scaling & Sample Selection\" — 将 CISC/Self-Certainty/ReASC 集中讨论，明确 positioning：现有工作均面向 reasoning/QA 的离散答案，我们首次在 structured IE 上做系统信号对比并发现 correlation-selection gap\n157\t    - \"Consistency for Structured IE\" — 引 Nédellec & Xia 2026 作为同期工作，显式对比：surface matching vs structural metrics (SJ)；他们的 limitation 是我们的 motivation\n158\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n159\t\n160\t### R11: \"SJ+logprob ensemble missing\" (Dream 2 — both reviewers)\n161\t- **Status**: ⚠️ REVISED by exp_016_rerun_1024. Results:\n162\t  - Ensemble AUROC (5-fold CV LR): NER 0.666 ± 0.070, RE 0.662 ± 0.078\n163\t  - Best single signal EM: NER AUROC 0.749, RE AUROC 0.706\n164\t  - **Ensemble has NO advantage over best single signal** — EM alone outperforms the 5-signal logistic regression ensemble by +8.3pp (NER) and +4.4pp (RE)\n165\t  - **Interpretation**: With 1024-token clean data, EM captures nearly all discriminative information. The ensemble's inferior performance likely reflects overfitting in the 5-fold CV LR with correlated features. This further supports presenting EM as a simple, strong baseline within the structural consistency family.\n166\t- **Priority**: DONE — write into paper with honest interpretation (no ensemble advantage claim)\n167\t\n168\t### R12: \"No supervised upper bound / reward model comparison\" (Dream 2)\n169\t- **Mitigation**: Simple logistic regression on [SJ, FK, logprob, voting_conf, EM] as proxy for trained verifier (included in exp-016). Results show ensemble underperforms best single signal (EM), suggesting feature redundancy rather than complementarity. Full reward model training out of scope for this paper — discuss as future work.\n170\t- **Priority**: P1 (partially addressed by exp-016 ensemble)\n171\t\n172\t### R13: \"Headroom capture rate low\" (Dream 2)\n173\t- **Mitigation**: NER oracle 0.7758, greedy 0.6439, best signal (logprob) 0.6501 → captures 0.5% of headroom. RE oracle 0.5850, greedy 0.4042, best signal (greedy itself) → 0% capture. Discuss explicitly in paper. Contextualize vs other unsupervised TTS methods. Argue that the information-theoretic ceiling for unsupervised signals is unknown — our result establishes a baseline and documents the gap.\n174\t- **Priority**: P0, paper writing\n175\t\n176\t### R14: \"Cross-model validation thin — need more than 2×8B\" (Dream 2)\n177\t- **Mitigation**: exp-017 (LLaMA on CoNLL, P1). 70B model infeasible within GPU budget. Acknowledge as limitation.\n178\t- **Priority**: P1\n179\t\n180\t### R15: \"Log-prob definition ambiguity — Eq.1 vs best-of-N ranking\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n181\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must clarify: log-prob ranks among N candidates (each sample's generation log-prob), not just score greedy output. Cost comparison table must state \"all best-of-N require N forward passes; log-prob adds zero ranking overhead.\"\n182\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n183\t\n184\t### R16: \"Zero figures — data-rich paper with only tables\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n185\t- **Mitigation**: Paper Agent must include ≥3 figures: (1) selection curves (F1 vs N for each signal + oracle), (2) reliability diagram (calibration), (3) N-scaling or cost-effectiveness scatter. Data exists from exp-010/015.\n186\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n187\t\n188\t### R17: \"Diagnostic framework overclaimed — descriptive not prescriptive\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [M][W])\n189\t- **Mitigation**: Soften \"diagnostic framework\" to \"diagnostic analysis\" throughout. Current taxonomy (ceiling/floor/compound error) is descriptive. Either formalize with a priori metrics or reframe as empirical analysis.\n190\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n191\t\n192\t### R18: \"No discussion of when consistency WOULD help\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n193\t- **Mitigation**: Add discussion paragraph: consistency should outperform log-prob when (a) model calibration is poor (in-context learning without fine-tuning), (b) log-prob unavailable (closed-source APIs), (c) ensemble/mixture settings, (d) tasks where model is systematically overconfident.\n194\t- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n195\t\n196\t### R19: \"Negative result partially predictable for fine-tuned models\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n197\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must argue non-obviousness: (a) self-consistency demonstrably helps for reasoning tasks (Wang et al. 2023), (b) structured prediction has internal structure that surface metrics can't capture, (c) the DEGREE of log-prob's strength and the task-complexity boundary are not predictable a priori.\n198\t- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n199\t\n200\t## Venue Fit\n201\t\n202\tEMNLP is well-suited for:\n203\t- Systematic empirical comparison of confidence signals for structured prediction\n204\t- Diagnostic findings with principled explanations\n205\t- The \"comparison + boundary condition\" contribution pattern\n206\t\n207\tRisk assessment (post-1024-token correction + bootstrap):\n208\t- **Structural risks (三档一致)**: (1) novelty perceived as incremental, (2) related work thin, (3) single RE dataset. These are presentation/positioning issues, NOT data issues — fixable by Paper Agent.\n209\t- **Data-dependent risks**: The bootstrap test strengthened the correlation-selection gap narrative definitively — NER logprob +0.6pp is confirmed noise (p=0.39), making the \"Weak Selectors\" claim statistically rigorous rather than directional.\n210\t- **Confirmed strength**: Structural consistency family (EM/voting/SJ) >> logprob on quality estimation (AUROC 0.75 vs 0.58). Correlation-selection gap is now statistically confirmed with bootstrap CI.\n211\t- **Critical path**: Paper Agent (related work 35+ refs, 3+ figures, contribution reframe) > new GPU experiments."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14f41098-1a14-4cd2-befd-b73275d72bd6","uuid":"acf00201-c10c-407a-90f8-9201a9711c18","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:00:28.649Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T092545/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — struct_self_consist_ie\n\n> Updated 2026-05-15 — D070 REFRAMING: from \"gap finding\" to \"regime-specific bottleneck identification with controlled ablation\". Motivated by 6-round 3.0/5 plateau — Reviewer diagnosis: content ceiling, not framing ceiling. Adding free-form decoding ablation as breakthrough experiment.\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR May 2026)\n- Deadline: ARR May cycle, 2026-05-25\n\n## Core Claims (3 条, D070 重排)\n\n### Claim 1 (PRIMARY — Regime-Specific Selection Bottleneck)\nThe correlation-selection gap in structured IE is **caused by constrained decoding**. Under constrained decoding (Outlines/grammar-guided), logprob score compression makes per-sample ranking impossible: 60% of instances have within-sample logprob range < 0.05. Controlled ablation via free-form generation confirms the mechanism: removing constrained decoding recovers logprob variance and selection ability.\n\n**Two-layer argument**:\n- Layer 1 (definitional, noted not discovered): 4/5 signals are instance-level aggregates → cannot rank candidates by construction. This is a conceptual clarification of QE vs selection conflation in prior work, not an empirical finding.\n- Layer 2 (empirical, the core contribution): (a) Logprob — the only per-sample signal — fails due to score compression under constrained decoding. (b) Consensus-proximity/MBR strategies also fail despite success in MT (non-trivial). (c) **Free-form ablation**: removing constrained decoding recovers logprob discrimination → proves compression is the bottleneck, not an inherent IE limitation.\n\n**Key evidence (constrained)**:\n- Non-tied subset (40%): logprob selection +2.9pp vs greedy (p=0.01), within-instance ρ: 0.08→0.39\n- Full set: logprob +0.6pp, bootstrap p=0.39, Cohen's d=0.038 (negligible), 95% CI [-3.0, +4.2]pp\n- Oracle headroom: NER +13pp, RE +18pp → information exists but signals can't access it under constrained decoding\n\n**Key evidence (free-form ablation)** [PLANNED — exp_freeform_ablation]:\n- Hypothesis: Free-form generation on SciERC will show (a) wider logprob variance, (b) improved logprob selection performance\n- If confirmed: gap is regime-specific → constrained decoding is the bottleneck\n- If not: gap is inherent to structured IE → stronger universal finding\n\n**Implications**: Not just \"signals don't work\" but \"here's WHY and WHEN they don't work, and here's a path forward\" (relaxed decoding + post-hoc filtering, or use logprob on non-tied subset).\n\n### Claim 2 (METHODOLOGY — QE Evaluation Framework)\nSystematic evaluation of 5 confidence signals across 4 families for structured IE quality estimation. This is the methodological infrastructure, not a primary contribution.\n\n**Key results**:\n- NER: EM AUROC 0.749, voting_conf ρ=0.379, SJ ρ=0.360 — all >> logprob (AUROC 0.578, ρ=0.205)\n- RE (preliminary, single benchmark): voting_conf leads both full and conditional\n- Difficulty-dependent signal ranking: WNUT-17 conditional collapse (ρ significant → n.s.) + logprob ρ=−0.410 (non-obvious: overconfidence on OOD)\n- Temperature robustness: SJ Δρ=±0.01 vs FK Δρ=±0.06-0.09\n\n**Evidence preserved from original Claim 1** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0, exp_012_rerun_1024):\n- NER full (n=529): ρ — voting_conf 0.379, SJ 0.360, EM 0.295, FK 0.267, logprob 0.205; AUROC — EM 0.749, SJ 0.692, voting_conf 0.684, FK 0.629, logprob 0.578\n- RE full (n=397): AUROC — EM 0.706, voting_conf 0.694, SJ 0.670, FK 0.609, logprob 0.601\n- ECE (NER): EM 0.353, voting 0.381, SJ 0.453, FK 0.451, logprob 0.706\n\n### Claim 2b (Selection evidence)\n**exp_016_rerun_1024 evidence** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0):\n- NER best-of-N (n=529): logprob 0.6501 > sj 0.6450 = ensemble 0.6450 > greedy 0.6439 > voting 0.6337 > random 0.6077 (oracle 0.7758)\n- RE best-of-N (n=397): greedy 0.4042 > logprob 0.3948 > sj 0.3855 = ensemble 0.3855 > voting 0.3592 > random 0.3544 (oracle 0.5850)\n\n**exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap evidence** (3-seed bootstrap, 1000 iterations):\n- NER logprob vs greedy: bootstrap 95% CI [−0.030, +0.042], permutation p=0.39\n- Effect size: Cohen's d=0.038 (negligible), sign test win rate=0.466\n\n### Claim 3 (Diagnostic — task-complexity boundary)\nThe effectiveness of consistency-based confidence is governed by task structural complexity: compound error propagation in relational tasks degrades the consistency-accuracy correlation on the full instance set, but the signal remains valid within the model's capability range. This boundary applies across all confidence signals tested.\n\n**MVP evidence**: RE full vs cond AUROC lift — EM: 0.706→0.752 (+4.6pp), SJ: 0.670→0.646 (−2.4pp, 待确认), voting_conf: 0.694→0.642 (−5.2pp, 待确认). Component decomposition shows all RE components equally weak (head_sj rho=0.210). T=0.7 naturally separates knowledge-gap vs uncertainty errors.\n\n**exp-005 evidence**: Conditional filtering dwarfs temperature tuning — RE SJ cond lift +0.07~0.14 vs temperature effect ±0.01. T=1.0 preserves more oracle headroom (RE: 0.167 vs 0.131) and diversity (1-SJ: 0.389 vs 0.313). Recommendation: T=1.0 + conditional filtering, not temperature optimization.\n\n**exp-001 N-scaling evidence** (SciERC, n=200 subset, ⚠️ needs full-set confirmation):\n- RE N=16: voting_conf ρ=0.448 (vs N=8 0.340, +0.108), SJ ρ=0.333 (vs 0.244, +0.089), all signals improve +0.07~0.10\n- NER N=16: flat (already saturated at N=8) — voting_conf 0.401 vs 0.392\n- **Key insight**: The task-complexity boundary is partially a SAMPLE BUDGET boundary. Compound error propagation increases per-instance variance, requiring more samples (N=16 vs N=8) to average out noise. This makes Claim 2 more nuanced: RE consistency fails at N=8 not because the signal is absent, but because it's noisier and needs more samples to manifest.\n- ⚠️ Caveat: exp-001 ran on 200/529 instances. Full-set replication needed before claiming in paper.\n\n## Story Spine (D070 REFRAMED)\n\n**Problem**: Test-time scaling via multi-sample generation improves LLM reasoning, but its effectiveness for structured information extraction is unclear. Practitioners need to know: can confidence signals select better outputs from multiple candidates?\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-consistency (Wang et al. 2023) succeeds for discrete-answer reasoning. MBR decoding succeeds for MT. But structured IE outputs (entity sets, relation triples) under constrained decoding present a fundamentally different challenge — and prior work conflates quality estimation with selection.\n\n**Our framing (D070 reposition — from \"finding a gap\" to \"identifying and verifying a bottleneck\")**:\n\nWe systematically compare five confidence signals for IE under constrained decoding, and discover a **regime-specific selection bottleneck**:\n1. **Conceptual clarification**: Four of five signals are instance-level by construction and cannot rank candidates — this is noted as a definitional property, not discovered empirically. The interesting question is whether the remaining strategies (logprob, MBR/consensus-proximity) can select.\n2. **Core empirical finding**: Logprob — the only per-sample signal — fails due to score compression under constrained decoding (60% of instances have within-sample range < 0.05). Consensus-proximity/MBR also fails despite success in MT.\n3. **Controlled verification**: Free-form decoding ablation confirms the mechanism — removing constrained decoding recovers logprob's discriminative power. The gap is regime-specific, not inherent to structured IE.\n4. **Practical pathway**: Non-tied instances (+2.9pp, p=0.01) show logprob works when compression is absent → actionable mitigation via relaxed decoding or non-tied subset selection.\n\n**Headline**: \"We identify, diagnose, and experimentally verify a regime-specific selection bottleneck in constrained-decoding IE: confidence signals that reliably predict output quality (AUROC 0.75) cannot select better candidates because constrained decoding compresses log-probability scores. A controlled free-form ablation confirms the mechanism and points to relaxed decoding as a mitigation path.\"\n\n**Potential title**: \"The Constrained Decoding Bottleneck: Why Confidence Signals Predict but Cannot Select in Information Extraction\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1: \"Only one NER dataset — generalization unclear\"\n- **Mitigation**: 2 datasets (SciERC + CoNLL-2003) × 2 models (Qwen3 + LLaMA) = 4 NER configurations. exp_017_llama_conll_infer SJ ρ=0.431 matches Qwen CoNLL ρ=0.436, demonstrating cross-model × cross-dataset consistency. Limitation: informal text domains (social media etc.) not covered — acknowledge in Limitations section.\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R2: \"Only one model family (Qwen3-8B)\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-007 (LLaMA-3.1-8B) shows model-agnostic effect\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R3: \"FK is a strawman baseline — what about log-prob, USC, exact-match?\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-012 (log-prob), exp-013 (exact-match), exp-014 (entity voting) provide comprehensive baseline comparison. Results: structural consistency family (EM+SJ+voting) >> log-prob >> FK. USC discussed in related work (LLM-as-judge, orthogonal approach).\n- **Priority**: P0, RESOLVED — results decisive\n\n### R3b: \"EM beats voting_conf and SJ on AUROC — why present SJ/voting_conf?\"\n- **Mitigation**: EM is a strict binary signal (all-or-nothing match); SJ captures partial agreement and generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs (relations, events). Voting_conf provides granular entity-level scores. NER full AUROC: EM 0.749 > SJ 0.692 > voting_conf 0.684, but ρ: voting_conf 0.379 > SJ 0.360 > EM 0.295. EM excels at binary discrimination but underperforms on rank ordering. SJ is also more temperature-robust (Δρ=±0.01). Paper presents all three as complementary instantiations of the structural consistency principle: EM for go/no-go filtering, voting_conf for ranking, SJ for generalizability.\n- **Priority**: P1 — narrative adjusted for 1024-token results\n\n### R4: \"No actual TTS improvement demonstrated\"\n- **Status**: ✅ CONFIRMED by exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap. No signal significantly outperforms greedy on either task. NER logprob +0.6pp not significant (bootstrap p=0.39, 95% CI [−0.030, +0.042], Cohen's d=0.038). RE: greedy > all signals.\n- **Mitigation**: Paper PIVOTS to \"confidence estimation + correlation-selection gap analysis.\" exp-006 redesigned as diagnostic: show selection curves to visualize the gap (F1 vs N per signal + oracle ceiling). The gap itself is a contribution, not a failure.\n- **Priority**: P0 — narrative pivot complete, bootstrap confirms\n\n### R5: \"Sample size N=8 may be too small for reliable SJ estimation\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-001 (N=16) with multi-seed robustness\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R6: \"Conditional analysis cherry-picks favorable instances\"\n- **Mitigation**: Principled separation (knowledge-gap vs uncertainty). Add threshold sensitivity analysis. Temperature analysis provides independent validation.\n- **Priority**: P0 (add sensitivity analysis)\n\n### R7: \"Only ρ as evaluation metric\"\n- **Mitigation**: Add AUROC, calibration plots (ECE), Kendall's τ for all experiments. ECE data now available: NER best calibrated = EM (0.353), RE best = voting (0.272). Logprob worst calibrated (NER 0.706, RE 0.769).\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R8: \"Formula-implementation discrepancy\"\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must describe actual algorithm (type-grouped Hungarian matching with max(|g_a|,|g_b|) denominator)\n- **Priority**: P0, paper writing fix\n\n### R9: \"Evaluation circularity (T>0 consistency vs T=0 F1)\"\n- **Mitigation**: Add leave-one-out SJ evaluation as robustness check. Justify cross-mode design (greedy = deterministic reference, standard in TTS literature).\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R10: \"Insufficient related work\" (三档一致 [B][M][W])\n- **Mitigation**: Expand to 35+ references. Must cite:\n  - USC (Chen 2024) — empirical differentiation, not just citation\n  - Semantic uncertainty (Kuhn 2023), calibration (Kadavath 2022, Guo 2017, Desai & Durrett 2020)\n  - **Conformal prediction for structured outputs**: Fisch et al. 2021, Angelopoulos et al. 2021, Bates et al. 2021\n  - **Token-level NER uncertainty**: Xiao & Wang 2019, Shelmanov et al. 2021, He et al. 2020\n  - **Ensemble/MC-dropout**: Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017, Gal & Ghahramani 2016\n  - **Verifier/reward models**: Cobbe et al. 2021, Lightman et al. 2023\n  - **TTS scaling theory**: Snell et al. 2024, Brown et al. 2024\n  - **Structured calibration**: Kuleshov & Liang 2015, Jagannatha & Yu 2022\n  - **IE confidence**: Culotta & McCallum 2004\n  - SelfCheckGPT (Manakul 2023), selective prediction (Geifman & El-Yaniv 2017)\n  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 必引]**:\n    - CISC (ACL Findings 2025) — confidence-weighted majority vote for reasoning; 对比：我们用 structural similarity 而非 confidence 加权，且面向 set-structured IE 输出\n    - Self-Certainty Best-of-N (ICLR 2026, arxiv 2502.18581) — KL-divergence reward-free selection; 对比：我们发现 log-prob 是唯一有效 selection signal (与其方向互补)，且揭示 correlation-selection gap\n    - ReASC (2026, arxiv 2601.02970) — reliability-aware adaptive self-consistency; 对比：仍限于 reasoning 离散答案\n    - Atomic Self-Consistency (EMNLP 2024) — 子声明级一致性 for long-form text; 对比：我们在 entity-set 级别做结构化度量\n    - **Nédellec & Xia (Genomics Informatics, 2026-02, PMC12888769)** — \"Consistency–accuracy correlation in hard-prompted LLMs for entity and relation extraction\"。最直接竞争者：4 LLMs 在植物健康 NER/RE 上研究 consistency-accuracy 相关性。**关键差异**：(a) 他们用 surface-level string matching，自承\"overlooks semantically consistent outputs\"，我们的 SJ 正好解决此问题; (b) 不研究 best-of-N selection; (c) 单领域 hard-prompted (T=0); (d) 无多信号家族对比。论文 Intro 可引用其 limitation 作为 SJ 的动机\n  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 应引]**:\n    - UQ for LLMs Survey (ACL Findings 2025) — 最全面 LLM 不确定性综述\n    - UQ+Calibration Survey (arxiv 2503.15850, 2025) — 第二篇综合综述\n    - Semantic Entropy Probes (2024) — 低成本不确定性估计\n    - Latent Self-Consistency (2025, arxiv 2508.18395) — embedding 空间一致性\n    - Ranked Voting SC (2025, arxiv 2505.10772) — 排名投票变体，仍限于推理任务\n    - Know Your Limits: Abstention Survey (TACL 2025) — 选择性预测综述，与 Claim 1 selective prediction 角度直接相关\n    - Confidence Estimation Survey (NAACL 2024, arxiv 2311.08298) — LLM 置信度估计全景定位\n    - **CoCoA (Vashurin et al., NeurIPS 2025, arxiv 2502.04964)** — MBR 框架融合 confidence+consistency 做 UQ，在 QA/摘要/翻译上评估。与我们 exp-016 ensemble (SJ+logprob) 对标，但未涉及 structured IE\n    - **Vashurin et al. (arxiv 2510.20460, 2025)** — VCE/MSP/Sample Consistency/CoCoA 四方法系统评估，任务不含 structured IE\n  - **需新增 Related Work 小节**:\n    - \"Test-Time Scaling & Sample Selection\" — 将 CISC/Self-Certainty/ReASC 集中讨论，明确 positioning：现有工作均面向 reasoning/QA 的离散答案，我们首次在 structured IE 上做系统信号对比并发现 correlation-selection gap\n    - \"Consistency for Structured IE\" — 引 Nédellec & Xia 2026 作为同期工作，显式对比：surface matching vs structural metrics (SJ)；他们的 limitation 是我们的 motivation\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R11: \"SJ+logprob ensemble missing\" (Dream 2 — both reviewers)\n- **Status**: ⚠️ REVISED by exp_016_rerun_1024. Results:\n  - Ensemble AUROC (5-fold CV LR): NER 0.666 ± 0.070, RE 0.662 ± 0.078\n  - Best single signal EM: NER AUROC 0.749, RE AUROC 0.706\n  - **Ensemble has NO advantage over best single signal** — EM alone outperforms the 5-signal logistic regression ensemble by +8.3pp (NER) and +4.4pp (RE)\n  - **Interpretation**: With 1024-token clean data, EM captures nearly all discriminative information. The ensemble's inferior performance likely reflects overfitting in the 5-fold CV LR with correlated features. This further supports presenting EM as a simple, strong baseline within the structural consistency family.\n- **Priority**: DONE — write into paper with honest interpretation (no ensemble advantage claim)\n\n### R12: \"No supervised upper bound / reward model comparison\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: Simple logistic regression on [SJ, FK, logprob, voting_conf, EM] as proxy for trained verifier (included in exp-016). Results show ensemble underperforms best single signal (EM), suggesting feature redundancy rather than complementarity. Full reward model training out of scope for this paper — discuss as future work.\n- **Priority**: P1 (partially addressed by exp-016 ensemble)\n\n### R13: \"Headroom capture rate low\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: NER oracle 0.7758, greedy 0.6439, best signal (logprob) 0.6501 → captures 0.5% of headroom. RE oracle 0.5850, greedy 0.4042, best signal (greedy itself) → 0% capture. Discuss explicitly in paper. Contextualize vs other unsupervised TTS methods. Argue that the information-theoretic ceiling for unsupervised signals is unknown — our result establishes a baseline and documents the gap.\n- **Priority**: P0, paper writing\n\n### R14: \"Cross-model validation thin — need more than 2×8B\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: exp-017 (LLaMA on CoNLL, P1). 70B model infeasible within GPU budget. Acknowledge as limitation.\n- **Priority**: P1\n\n### R15: \"Log-prob definition ambiguity — Eq.1 vs best-of-N ranking\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must clarify: log-prob ranks among N candidates (each sample's generation log-prob), not just score greedy output. Cost comparison table must state \"all best-of-N require N forward passes; log-prob adds zero ranking overhead.\"\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R16: \"Zero figures — data-rich paper with only tables\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper Agent must include ≥3 figures: (1) selection curves (F1 vs N for each signal + oracle), (2) reliability diagram (calibration), (3) N-scaling or cost-effectiveness scatter. Data exists from exp-010/015.\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R17: \"Diagnostic framework overclaimed — descriptive not prescriptive\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [M][W])\n- **Mitigation**: Soften \"diagnostic framework\" to \"diagnostic analysis\" throughout. Current taxonomy (ceiling/floor/compound error) is descriptive. Either formalize with a priori metrics or reframe as empirical analysis.\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R18: \"No discussion of when consistency WOULD help\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Add discussion paragraph: consistency should outperform log-prob when (a) model calibration is poor (in-context learning without fine-tuning), (b) log-prob unavailable (closed-source APIs), (c) ensemble/mixture settings, (d) tasks where model is systematically overconfident.\n- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R19: \"Negative result partially predictable for fine-tuned models\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must argue non-obviousness: (a) self-consistency demonstrably helps for reasoning tasks (Wang et al. 2023), (b) structured prediction has internal structure that surface metrics can't capture, (c) the DEGREE of log-prob's strength and the task-complexity boundary are not predictable a priori.\n- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n\n## Venue Fit\n\nEMNLP is well-suited for:\n- Systematic empirical comparison of confidence signals for structured prediction\n- Diagnostic findings with principled explanations\n- The \"comparison + boundary condition\" contribution pattern\n\nRisk assessment (post-1024-token correction + bootstrap):\n- **Structural risks (三档一致)**: (1) novelty perceived as incremental, (2) related work thin, (3) single RE dataset. These are presentation/positioning issues, NOT data issues — fixable by Paper Agent.\n- **Data-dependent risks**: The bootstrap test strengthened the correlation-selection gap narrative definitively — NER logprob +0.6pp is confirmed noise (p=0.39), making the \"Weak Selectors\" claim statistically rigorous rather than directional.\n- **Confirmed strength**: Structural consistency family (EM/voting/SJ) >> logprob on quality estimation (AUROC 0.75 vs 0.58). Correlation-selection gap is now statistically confirmed with bootstrap CI.\n- **Critical path**: Paper Agent (related work 35+ refs, 3+ figures, contribution reframe) > new GPU experiments.","numLines":211,"startLine":1,"totalLines":211}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0146EDviE3LT7bJPufDKHAtS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"freeform_decoding_ablation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"移除 Outlines constrained decoding，对 SciERC NER+RE 生成 8 个 free-form samples/instance。 对比 constrained vs free-form 的 logprob variance、selection F1、QE 指标。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"freeform_parse_rate_ner\": 0.72,\n7\t      \"freeform_parse_rate_re\": 0.65,\n8\t      \"freeform_n_valid_ner\": 381,\n9\t      \"freeform_n_valid_re\": 258,\n10\t      \"constrained_logprob_range_median\": 0.03,\n11\t      \"freeform_logprob_range_median\": 0.07,\n12\t      \"freeform_logprob_range_iqr\": [\n13\t        0.03,\n14\t        0.14\n15\t      ],\n16\t      \"pct_instances_range_lt_005_constrained\": 0.6,\n17\t      \"pct_instances_range_lt_005_freeform\": 0.38,\n18\t      \"constrained_logprob_rho_ner\": 0.205,\n19\t      \"freeform_logprob_rho_ner\": 0.22,\n20\t      \"freeform_logprob_rho_ner_p\": 4e-05,\n21\t      \"constrained_logprob_rho_re\": 0.266,\n22\t      \"freeform_logprob_rho_re\": 0.19,\n23\t      \"freeform_logprob_rho_re_p\": 0.002,\n24\t      \"constrained_logprob_auroc_ner\": 0.578,\n25\t      \"freeform_logprob_auroc_ner\": 0.57,\n26\t      \"constrained_logprob_auroc_re\": 0.6,\n27\t      \"freeform_logprob_auroc_re\": 0.56,\n28\t      \"constrained_greedy_f1_ner\": 0.644,\n29\t      \"freeform_greedy_f1_ner\": 0.631,\n30\t      \"freeform_logprob_selection_f1_ner\": 0.634,\n31\t      \"freeform_logprob_selection_delta_vs_greedy_ner_pp\": 0.3,\n32\t      \"freeform_logprob_selection_p_ner\": 0.42,\n33\t      \"constrained_greedy_f1_re\": 0.403,\n34\t      \"freeform_greedy_f1_re\": 0.382,\n35\t      \"freeform_logprob_selection_f1_re\": 0.379,\n36\t      \"freeform_logprob_selection_delta_vs_greedy_re_pp\": -0.3,\n37\t      \"freeform_logprob_selection_p_re\": 0.65,\n38\t      \"freeform_oracle_f1_ner\": 0.74,\n39\t      \"freeform_oracle_headroom_ner\": 0.109,\n40\t      \"freeform_oracle_f1_re\": 0.53,\n41\t      \"freeform_oracle_headroom_re\": 0.148,\n42\t      \"parseable_subset_mean_greedy_f1_ner\": 0.68,\n43\t      \"full_set_mean_greedy_f1_ner\": 0.644,\n44\t      \"parseable_subset_mean_greedy_f1_re\": 0.44,\n45\t      \"full_set_mean_greedy_f1_re\": 0.403,\n46\t      \"freeform_sj_rho_ner\": 0.34,\n47\t      \"freeform_voting_conf_rho_ner\": 0.36,\n48\t      \"freeform_sj_rho_re\": 0.21,\n49\t      \"freeform_selection_delta_ci95_ner\": [\n50\t        -0.025,\n51\t        0.031\n52\t      ],\n53\t      \"freeform_selection_delta_ci95_re\": [\n54\t        -0.035,\n55\t        0.029\n56\t      ],\n57\t      \"freeform_cohen_d_ner\": 0.04,\n58\t      \"freeform_cohen_d_re\": -0.03\n59\t    },\n60\t    \"tables\": [\n61\t      {\n62\t        \"name\": \"Table: Constrained vs Free-form Logprob Comparison\",\n63\t        \"columns\": [\n64\t          \"Metric\",\n65\t          \"Constrained\",\n66\t          \"Free-form\",\n67\t          \"Δ\",\n68\t          \"p-value\"\n69\t        ],\n70\t        \"rows\": [\n71\t          [\n72\t            \"NER logprob range median\",\n73\t            \"0.03\",\n74\t            \"0.07\",\n75\t            \"+0.04\",\n76\t            \"<0.001\"\n77\t          ],\n78\t          [\n79\t            \"NER logprob ρ(F1)\",\n80\t            \"0.205\",\n81\t            \"0.22\",\n82\t            \"+0.015\",\n83\t            \"—\"\n84\t          ],\n85\t          [\n86\t            \"NER logprob AUROC\",\n87\t            \"0.578\",\n88\t            \"0.57\",\n89\t            \"−0.008\",\n90\t            \"—\"\n91\t          ],\n92\t          [\n93\t            \"NER logprob selection F1\",\n94\t            \"0.650\",\n95\t            \"0.634\",\n96\t            \"−0.016\",\n97\t            \"—\"\n98\t          ],\n99\t          [\n100\t            \"NER selection Δ vs greedy (pp)\",\n101\t            \"+0.6\",\n102\t            \"+0.3\",\n103\t            \"−0.3\",\n104\t            \"0.42\"\n105\t          ],\n106\t          [\n107\t            \"RE logprob range median\",\n108\t            \"0.02\",\n109\t            \"0.06\",\n110\t            \"+0.04\",\n111\t            \"<0.001\"\n112\t          ],\n113\t          [\n114\t            \"RE logprob ρ(F1)\",\n115\t            \"0.266\",\n116\t            \"0.19\",\n117\t            \"−0.076\",\n118\t            \"—\"\n119\t          ],\n120\t          [\n121\t            \"RE logprob AUROC\",\n122\t            \"0.600\",\n123\t            \"0.56\",\n124\t            \"−0.040\",\n125\t            \"—\"\n126\t          ],\n127\t          [\n128\t            \"RE selection Δ vs greedy (pp)\",\n129\t            \"+0.7\",\n130\t            \"−0.3\",\n131\t            \"−1.0\",\n132\t            \"0.65\"\n133\t          ]\n134\t        ]\n135\t      },\n136\t      {\n137\t        \"name\": \"Table: Parse Rate and Selection Bias\",\n138\t        \"columns\": [\n139\t          \"Subset\",\n140\t          \"NER n\",\n141\t          \"NER mean F1\",\n142\t          \"RE n\",\n143\t          \"RE mean F1\"\n144\t        ],\n145\t        \"rows\": [\n146\t          [\n147\t            \"Full set (constrained)\",\n148\t            \"529\",\n149\t            \"0.644\",\n150\t            \"397\",\n151\t            \"0.403\"\n152\t          ],\n153\t          [\n154\t            \"Parseable (free-form)\",\n155\t            \"381\",\n156\t            \"0.680\",\n157\t            \"258\",\n158\t            \"0.440\"\n159\t          ],\n160\t          [\n161\t            \"Unparseable (free-form)\",\n162\t            \"148\",\n163\t            \"0.551\",\n164\t            \"139\",\n165\t            \"0.334\"\n166\t          ]\n167\t        ]\n168\t      }\n169\t    ],\n170\t    \"figures\": [],\n171\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-018 在 worst 档下产生的是一个 well-designed null result：controlled ablation 证明 score compression 不是 selection 失败的 root cause。这既是坏消息（D070 reframing 的核心因果叙事被否定） 也是好消息（universal negative finding 比 regime-specific finding 更有 generality）。\\n但叙事需要第二次 pivot。新的 argument structure： (1) IE output 是 set-of-sets（entity set × relation set），组合空间使得任何 instance-level scalar signal 的排序能力存在 information-theoretic 上限——一个数字无法 encode \\\"which entities are correct and which are not\\\"； (2) 与 reasoning/QA 的离散答案空间形成 structural contrast：self-consistency 在 QA 上成功 恰因答案空间小（majority vote 在 5-10 个 candidate 中选）； (3) QE 仍然有效（AUROC 0.75）说明 signals 捕捉了 instance difficulty，但无法区分 same-difficulty 内的 quality variation。\\n关键风险：parse rate 偏低 + selection bias 使得 null result 的说服力打折扣。 Reviewer 可能 argue \\\"你的 free-form 实验 underpowered（n=381 NER, n=258 RE）， 且 parseable subset 本身偏向 easy instances\\\"。需要在 paper 中做 sensitivity analysis （only on instances where all 8 free-form samples parse），并 acknowledge limitation。\\nExpected reviewer score 在此档下降到 2.5-3.0 区间。Findings 接收概率 10-25%。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档的核心逻辑：constrained decoding 确实压缩了 logprob range（中位数 0.03），移除约束后 range 上升到 0.07——但这远不够。0.07 的 range 意味着 8 个 sample 的 logprob 仍然聚集在一个 很窄的带内，无法有效区分质量差异。原因在于：fine-tuned 8B 模型在 SciERC 上的 output distribution 本身就很 peaked——不论是否有 grammar constraint，模型对于给定 input 的 \\\"preferred output mode\\\" 高度集中。Constrained decoding 只是略微加剧了已经存在的低 entropy 问题。\\nParse rate 仅 ~70% 是因为 fine-tuning 时用了 constrained decoding 作为 training-time format guarantee，模型并未充分学会 JSON format 的内在结构。更关键的是，parseable subset 偏向 easy instances（mean greedy F1 0.68 vs full set 0.644），因为 format-compliant 的 free-form output 更可能出现在模型 \\\"confident\\\" 的 instances 上——这些恰恰是 oracle headroom 更小、selection 价值更低的 instances。\\nSelection F1 几乎不变（NER +0.3pp, p=0.42; RE -0.3pp, p=0.65）直接否定了 bottleneck 假说。 如果 score compression 是 selection 失败的主因，那么恢复 variance 应该恢复 selection——但没有。 这说明 logprob 作为 scalar signal 的排序失败不是因为被压缩，而是因为 IE 的 set-valued output 空间中，generation probability 与 output quality（F1）之间本就不存在强的单调关系。一个 sample 可以有高 logprob（模型 confident）但 F1 低（confident about wrong entities），也可以有低 logprob （探索性 output）但 F1 高（偶然命中更多 gold entities）。\\nRE 更差是因为 free-form 下 relation format 的 parse failure 更高（35%），且 RE 的组合空间 (entity pairs × relation types) 远大于 NER，使得 scalar signal 的信息论上限更低。\\n\"\n172\t  },\n173\t  {\n174\t    \"name\": \"ner_llama_conll\",\n175\t    \"description\": \"LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003 进行 NER inference (N=8, T=1.0)。 Cross-model × cross-dataset validation，强化 model-agnostic claim。\\n\",\n176\t    \"results\": {\n177\t      \"greedy_f1\": 0.918,\n178\t      \"oracle_f1\": 0.945,\n179\t      \"oracle_headroom\": 0.027,\n180\t      \"n_instances\": 3453,\n181\t      \"n_valid\": 2756,\n182\t      \"sj_rho_full\": 0.43,\n183\t      \"fk_rho_full\": 0.42,\n184\t      \"logprob_rho_full\": 0.31,\n185\t      \"em_rho_full\": 0.43,\n186\t      \"voting_conf_rho_full\": 0.42,\n187\t      \"sj_auroc_full\": 0.7,\n188\t      \"logprob_auroc_full\": 0.76,\n189\t      \"logprob_selection_f1\": 0.919,\n190\t      \"sj_selection_f1\": 0.916,\n191\t      \"voting_selection_f1\": 0.917,\n192\t      \"random_selection_f1\": 0.912,\n193\t      \"oracle_f1_selection\": 0.945,\n194\t      \"qwen_conll_sj_rho\": 0.436,\n195\t      \"llama_conll_sj_rho\": 0.43,\n196\t      \"delta_sj_rho\": -0.006\n197\t    },\n198\t    \"tables\": [\n199\t      {\n200\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model QE Comparison on CoNLL-2003\",\n201\t        \"columns\": [\n202\t          \"Signal\",\n203\t          \"Qwen ρ\",\n204\t          \"LLaMA ρ\",\n205\t          \"Δρ\",\n206\t          \"Qwen AUROC\",\n207\t          \"LLaMA AUROC\"\n208\t        ],\n209\t        \"rows\": [\n210\t          [\n211\t            \"SJ\",\n212\t            \"0.436\",\n213\t            \"0.43\",\n214\t            \"−0.006\",\n215\t            \"0.80\",\n216\t            \"0.70\"\n217\t          ],\n218\t          [\n219\t            \"FK\",\n220\t            \"0.400\",\n221\t            \"0.42\",\n222\t            \"+0.020\",\n223\t            \"0.77\",\n224\t            \"0.70\"\n225\t          ],\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"logprob\",\n228\t            \"0.316\",\n229\t            \"0.31\",\n230\t            \"−0.006\",\n231\t            \"0.75\",\n232\t            \"0.76\"\n233\t          ],\n234\t          [\n235\t            \"EM\",\n236\t            \"0.451\",\n237\t            \"0.43\",\n238\t            \"−0.021\",\n239\t            \"0.82\",\n240\t            \"0.70\"\n241\t          ],\n242\t          [\n243\t            \"voting_conf\",\n244\t            \"0.424\",\n245\t            \"0.42\",\n246\t            \"−0.004\",\n247\t            \"0.79\",\n248\t            \"0.71\"\n249\t          ]\n250\t        ]\n251\t      }\n252\t    ],\n253\t    \"figures\": [],\n254\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model validation 成功但对 worst 档的核心困境帮助不大。可以作为 Table 1 的一行补充 model-agnostic evidence，但不改变 selection failure 的 narrative。在 worst 档的 paper 中，这个实验从 \\\"strengthening the bottleneck claim\\\" 降级为 \\\"confirming QE generalization\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档对 exp-017 的影响有限——这个实验是 cross-model validation，不直接依赖 bottleneck 假说。 CoNLL-2003 是 \\\"easy\\\" NER dataset（greedy F1 ~0.92），oracle headroom 仅 ~0.027， selection 的理论上限就很低。LLaMA 在 CoNLL 上的表现应与 Qwen 高度一致 （exp_017_llama_conll_infer 已有 SJ ρ=0.431 的数据佐证），因为两个 8B 模型在 well-studied benchmark 上的 behavior 趋同。\\n在 worst 档下，这个实验的结果本身是 \\\"positive\\\"（cross-model consistency confirmed）， 但对论文的帮助有限：它只证明了 QE 信号的 model-agnostic property，而 worst 档的核心问题 是 selection 失败的叙事需要 pivot。Cross-model validation 对 \\\"fundamental hardness\\\" 叙事是中性的——不增强也不削弱。\\nSelection F1 在 CoNLL 上接近 greedy（+0.1pp），与 SciERC 的 pattern 一致。 但因为 headroom 只有 2.7pp，即使 oracle 也只能提升这么多，所以 selection failure 在 CoNLL 上的 diagnostic value 很低。\\n\"\n255\t  },\n256\t  {\n257\t    \"name\": \"ner_ood_robustness\",\n258\t    \"description\": \"在 OOD 条件下（cross-domain transfer）测试 NER consistency signal 的鲁棒性。 依赖 exp-003 (WNUT-17) 的 fine-tuned model 做 domain shift 测试。\\n\",\n259\t    \"results\": {\n260\t      \"ood_greedy_f1\": 0.35,\n261\t      \"ood_oracle_f1\": 0.52,\n262\t      \"ood_headroom\": 0.17,\n263\t      \"ood_sj_rho_full\": 0.05,\n264\t      \"ood_fk_rho_full\": 0.08,\n265\t      \"ood_logprob_rho_full\": -0.3,\n266\t      \"ood_voting_conf_rho_full\": 0.09,\n267\t      \"ood_sj_auroc\": 0.53,\n268\t      \"ood_logprob_auroc\": 0.42,\n269\t      \"ood_sample_f1_pct_zero\": 62.0,\n270\t      \"ood_n_instances\": 1287,\n271\t      \"ood_logprob_negative_rho\": true,\n272\t      \"ood_logprob_overconfidence_on_wrong\": true\n273\t    },\n274\t    \"tables\": [\n275\t      {\n276\t        \"name\": \"Table: In-domain vs OOD Signal Comparison\",\n277\t        \"columns\": [\n278\t          \"Signal\",\n279\t          \"In-domain ρ (SciERC)\",\n280\t          \"OOD ρ\",\n281\t          \"Δρ\"\n282\t        ],\n283\t        \"rows\": [\n284\t          [\n285\t            \"SJ\",\n286\t            \"0.36\",\n287\t            \"0.05\",\n288\t            \"−0.31\"\n289\t          ],\n290\t          [\n291\t            \"FK\",\n292\t            \"0.27\",\n293\t            \"0.08\",\n294\t            \"−0.19\"\n295\t          ],\n296\t          [\n297\t            \"logprob\",\n298\t            \"0.21\",\n299\t            \"−0.30\",\n300\t            \"−0.51\"\n301\t          ],\n302\t          [\n303\t            \"voting_conf\",\n304\t            \"0.38\",\n305\t            \"0.09\",\n306\t            \"−0.29\"\n307\t          ]\n308\t        ]\n309\t      }\n310\t    ],\n311\t    \"figures\": [],\n312\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD 实验在 worst 档下提供的额外信息有限——exp-003 WNUT-17 已经展示了同样的 pathology。 且 exp-003 status=orphaned，exp-011 依赖 exp-003，实际执行概率极低。 如果执行，它强化了 \\\"logprob is unreliable under shift\\\" 的 claim，但这不是论文的核心。 建议 worst 档下不投入 GPU hours 在这个实验上，将资源集中于 exp-018 的 robustness checks。\\n\\n\\nOOD 条件下所有信号急剧退化。Greedy F1 降到 ~0.35 意味着模型在目标域基本失效， >60% samples F1=0。在这个 regime 下： (1) SJ/FK/voting 的 ρ 接近 0 因为大部分 instances 的 N 个 samples 全部 F1=0， 无 variance 可供 correlation 捕捉； (2) Logprob 出现 WNUT-17 同样的 pathology：ρ 为负（-0.30），模型对 OOD 输入 过度自信——logprob 高的 samples 反而更差，因为模型 \\\"confidently\\\" 产出 in-domain patterns 而非 target domain 的正确 entities； (3) 这与 exp-003 (WNUT-17 logprob ρ=-0.41) 的发现一致。\\n在 worst 档下，这个实验的解读方向改变：不再是 \\\"OOD shows limitations of consistency signals\\\" （这太 obvious），而是作为 \\\"logprob overconfidence under distribution shift\\\" 的额外证据， 支持 \\\"scalar signals fail for structural reasons, not just compression\\\" 的论点。 但 P2 priority + exp-003 已经 orphaned 意味着这个实验大概率不会执行。\\n\"\n313\t  },\n314\t  {\n315\t    \"name\": \"simple_verifier_baseline\",\n316\t    \"description\": \"训练 supervised verifier（DeBERTa-v3-large 或 Qwen3-8B classification head）在 existing (input, output, F1) 数据上。测试 verifier 能否部分 close selection gap， 为 unsupervised signal 的 failure 提供 upper bound。\\n\",\n317\t    \"results\": {\n318\t      \"train_n_instances\": 529,\n319\t      \"train_n_samples_per_instance\": 8,\n320\t      \"train_total_pairs\": 4232,\n321\t      \"train_val_split\": \"5-fold CV\",\n322\t      \"deberta_auroc_ner\": 0.72,\n323\t      \"deberta_auroc_re\": 0.66,\n324\t      \"deberta_selection_f1_ner\": 0.652,\n325\t      \"deberta_selection_delta_vs_greedy_ner_pp\": 0.8,\n326\t      \"deberta_selection_p_ner\": 0.18,\n327\t      \"deberta_selection_f1_re\": 0.398,\n328\t      \"deberta_selection_delta_vs_greedy_re_pp\": -0.5,\n329\t      \"deberta_selection_p_re\": 0.55,\n330\t      \"best_unsupervised_auroc_ner\": 0.749,\n331\t      \"deberta_vs_best_unsupervised_auroc_ner\": -0.029,\n332\t      \"best_unsupervised_selection_ner\": 0.65,\n333\t      \"deberta_vs_best_unsupervised_selection_ner\": 0.002,\n334\t      \"oracle_selection_f1_ner\": 0.776,\n335\t      \"oracle_selection_f1_re\": 0.588,\n336\t      \"verifier_headroom_capture_ner_pct\": 6.1,\n337\t      \"verifier_headroom_capture_re_pct\": 0.0\n338\t    },\n339\t    \"tables\": [\n340\t      {\n341\t        \"name\": \"Table: Supervised Verifier vs Unsupervised Signals\",\n342\t        \"columns\": [\n343\t          \"Method\",\n344\t          \"NER AUROC\",\n345\t          \"NER Sel. F1\",\n346\t          \"RE AUROC\",\n347\t          \"RE Sel. F1\"\n348\t        ],\n349\t        \"rows\": [\n350\t          [\n351\t            \"DeBERTa verifier (5-fold CV)\",\n352\t            \"0.72\",\n353\t            \"0.652\",\n354\t            \"0.66\",\n355\t            \"0.398\"\n356\t          ],\n357\t          [\n358\t            \"EM (best unsupervised AUROC)\",\n359\t            \"0.749\",\n360\t            \"0.650\",\n361\t            \"0.706\",\n362\t            \"0.403\"\n363\t          ],\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"Logprob (best unsupervised sel.)\",\n366\t            \"0.578\",\n367\t            \"0.650\",\n368\t            \"0.600\",\n369\t            \"0.410\"\n370\t          ],\n371\t          [\n372\t            \"Greedy baseline\",\n373\t            \"—\",\n374\t            \"0.644\",\n375\t            \"—\",\n376\t            \"0.403\"\n377\t          ],\n378\t          [\n379\t            \"Oracle\",\n380\t            \"—\",\n381\t            \"0.776\",\n382\t            \"—\",\n383\t            \"0.588\"\n384\t          ]\n385\t        ]\n386\t      }\n387\t    ],\n388\t    \"figures\": [],\n389\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-019 在 worst 档下的价值在于 closing the loop：即使 supervised signal 也无法显著 close selection gap，说明问题不在于 signal quality 而在于 task structure。但执行条件 苛刻（需要 exp-018 先完成 + 还有 DDL 前时间），且 4K training data 的 verifier 说服力 有限。建议：如果时间允许，作为 1 天 quick experiment 执行，结果写入 Discussion 而非 main results。如果时间不够，在 paper 中引用 exp-016 ensemble（logistic regression on 5 signals）作为 proxy supervised baseline，其 AUROC 0.735 已经 ≤ best single signal EM 0.749，传达同样的 message。\\n\\nWorst 档下 supervised verifier 也基本失败，原因有三层：\\n(1) 训练数据不足：529 instances × 8 samples = 4232 training pairs，对于 DeBERTa 这种 encoder 来说数据量极少。5-fold CV 下每折只有 ~3400 training pairs，严重 overfit 风险。 即使不 overfit，模型学到的更多是 \\\"哪些 input 难\\\"（instance difficulty）而非 \\\"哪个 output 好\\\"（within-instance quality variation），因为 inter-instance F1 variance 远大于 intra-instance F1 variance。\\n(2) Feature gap：DeBERTa 只能看到 (input, output) text pair，无法 access logprob 或 其他 generation metadata。它本质上在做 NLI-style 判断 \\\"output 是否合理\\\"，而 IE 的 \\\"合理性\\\" 需要 precise span matching，这超出了 encoder 的 zero-shot 能力。即使 fine-tune， 4K pairs 不足以学会 IE-specific quality patterns。\\n(3) IE 的组合复杂性：即使 verifier AUROC 达到 0.72（超过 logprob 的 0.578）， 这仍然是 instance-level discrimination（\\\"这个 instance 的 output 总体好不好\\\"）， 而非 within-instance ranking（\\\"这 8 个 candidate 中哪个最好\\\"）。 AUROC 0.72 不等于 selection 能力——exp-016 已经证明 AUROC 0.749 的 EM 信号 selection 也只有 +0.6pp（n.s.）。\\nVerifier 的 headroom capture rate 极低（NER 6.1%，RE 0%）与 unsupervised signals 的 pattern 一致，说明 selection gap 不是 \\\"signals 太弱\\\" 而是 \\\"task structure 使得 instance-level scoring 根本不够\\\"。这反而支持了 worst 档的核心论点：需要 sub-instance level 的 selection mechanism（如 entity-level MBR），scalar scoring 存在 fundamental ceiling。\\n但 reviewer 价值有限：verifier 没有显著超过 best unsupervised signal， \\\"supervised 也不行\\\" 这个 claim 在 4K training pairs 下 underpowered， reviewer 会 argue \\\"给足够数据 verifier 肯定能 work\\\"。\\n\"\n390\t  }\n391\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14f41098-1a14-4cd2-befd-b73275d72bd6","uuid":"fef1936d-961b-4fab-a98f-cc933e0a6c78","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:00:28.884Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T092545/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"freeform_decoding_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"移除 Outlines constrained decoding，对 SciERC NER+RE 生成 8 个 free-form samples/instance。 对比 constrained vs free-form 的 logprob variance、selection F1、QE 指标。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"freeform_parse_rate_ner\": 0.72,\n      \"freeform_parse_rate_re\": 0.65,\n      \"freeform_n_valid_ner\": 381,\n      \"freeform_n_valid_re\": 258,\n      \"constrained_logprob_range_median\": 0.03,\n      \"freeform_logprob_range_median\": 0.07,\n      \"freeform_logprob_range_iqr\": [\n        0.03,\n        0.14\n      ],\n      \"pct_instances_range_lt_005_constrained\": 0.6,\n      \"pct_instances_range_lt_005_freeform\": 0.38,\n      \"constrained_logprob_rho_ner\": 0.205,\n      \"freeform_logprob_rho_ner\": 0.22,\n      \"freeform_logprob_rho_ner_p\": 4e-05,\n      \"constrained_logprob_rho_re\": 0.266,\n      \"freeform_logprob_rho_re\": 0.19,\n      \"freeform_logprob_rho_re_p\": 0.002,\n      \"constrained_logprob_auroc_ner\": 0.578,\n      \"freeform_logprob_auroc_ner\": 0.57,\n      \"constrained_logprob_auroc_re\": 0.6,\n      \"freeform_logprob_auroc_re\": 0.56,\n      \"constrained_greedy_f1_ner\": 0.644,\n      \"freeform_greedy_f1_ner\": 0.631,\n      \"freeform_logprob_selection_f1_ner\": 0.634,\n      \"freeform_logprob_selection_delta_vs_greedy_ner_pp\": 0.3,\n      \"freeform_logprob_selection_p_ner\": 0.42,\n      \"constrained_greedy_f1_re\": 0.403,\n      \"freeform_greedy_f1_re\": 0.382,\n      \"freeform_logprob_selection_f1_re\": 0.379,\n      \"freeform_logprob_selection_delta_vs_greedy_re_pp\": -0.3,\n      \"freeform_logprob_selection_p_re\": 0.65,\n      \"freeform_oracle_f1_ner\": 0.74,\n      \"freeform_oracle_headroom_ner\": 0.109,\n      \"freeform_oracle_f1_re\": 0.53,\n      \"freeform_oracle_headroom_re\": 0.148,\n      \"parseable_subset_mean_greedy_f1_ner\": 0.68,\n      \"full_set_mean_greedy_f1_ner\": 0.644,\n      \"parseable_subset_mean_greedy_f1_re\": 0.44,\n      \"full_set_mean_greedy_f1_re\": 0.403,\n      \"freeform_sj_rho_ner\": 0.34,\n      \"freeform_voting_conf_rho_ner\": 0.36,\n      \"freeform_sj_rho_re\": 0.21,\n      \"freeform_selection_delta_ci95_ner\": [\n        -0.025,\n        0.031\n      ],\n      \"freeform_selection_delta_ci95_re\": [\n        -0.035,\n        0.029\n      ],\n      \"freeform_cohen_d_ner\": 0.04,\n      \"freeform_cohen_d_re\": -0.03\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Constrained vs Free-form Logprob Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Constrained\",\n          \"Free-form\",\n          \"Δ\",\n          \"p-value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"NER logprob range median\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.07\",\n            \"+0.04\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NER logprob ρ(F1)\",\n            \"0.205\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"+0.015\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NER logprob AUROC\",\n            \"0.578\",\n            \"0.57\",\n            \"−0.008\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NER logprob selection F1\",\n            \"0.650\",\n            \"0.634\",\n            \"−0.016\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NER selection Δ vs greedy (pp)\",\n            \"+0.6\",\n            \"+0.3\",\n            \"−0.3\",\n            \"0.42\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RE logprob range median\",\n            \"0.02\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"+0.04\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RE logprob ρ(F1)\",\n            \"0.266\",\n            \"0.19\",\n            \"−0.076\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RE logprob AUROC\",\n            \"0.600\",\n            \"0.56\",\n            \"−0.040\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RE selection Δ vs greedy (pp)\",\n            \"+0.7\",\n            \"−0.3\",\n            \"−1.0\",\n            \"0.65\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Parse Rate and Selection Bias\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Subset\",\n          \"NER n\",\n          \"NER mean F1\",\n          \"RE n\",\n          \"RE mean F1\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Full set (constrained)\",\n            \"529\",\n            \"0.644\",\n            \"397\",\n            \"0.403\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Parseable (free-form)\",\n            \"381\",\n            \"0.680\",\n            \"258\",\n            \"0.440\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Unparseable (free-form)\",\n            \"148\",\n            \"0.551\",\n            \"139\",\n            \"0.334\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-018 在 worst 档下产生的是一个 well-designed null result：controlled ablation 证明 score compression 不是 selection 失败的 root cause。这既是坏消息（D070 reframing 的核心因果叙事被否定） 也是好消息（universal negative finding 比 regime-specific finding 更有 generality）。\\n但叙事需要第二次 pivot。新的 argument structure： (1) IE output 是 set-of-sets（entity set × relation set），组合空间使得任何 instance-level scalar signal 的排序能力存在 information-theoretic 上限——一个数字无法 encode \\\"which entities are correct and which are not\\\"； (2) 与 reasoning/QA 的离散答案空间形成 structural contrast：self-consistency 在 QA 上成功 恰因答案空间小（majority vote 在 5-10 个 candidate 中选）； (3) QE 仍然有效（AUROC 0.75）说明 signals 捕捉了 instance difficulty，但无法区分 same-difficulty 内的 quality variation。\\n关键风险：parse rate 偏低 + selection bias 使得 null result 的说服力打折扣。 Reviewer 可能 argue \\\"你的 free-form 实验 underpowered（n=381 NER, n=258 RE）， 且 parseable subset 本身偏向 easy instances\\\"。需要在 paper 中做 sensitivity analysis （only on instances where all 8 free-form samples parse），并 acknowledge limitation。\\nExpected reviewer score 在此档下降到 2.5-3.0 区间。Findings 接收概率 10-25%。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档的核心逻辑：constrained decoding 确实压缩了 logprob range（中位数 0.03），移除约束后 range 上升到 0.07——但这远不够。0.07 的 range 意味着 8 个 sample 的 logprob 仍然聚集在一个 很窄的带内，无法有效区分质量差异。原因在于：fine-tuned 8B 模型在 SciERC 上的 output distribution 本身就很 peaked——不论是否有 grammar constraint，模型对于给定 input 的 \\\"preferred output mode\\\" 高度集中。Constrained decoding 只是略微加剧了已经存在的低 entropy 问题。\\nParse rate 仅 ~70% 是因为 fine-tuning 时用了 constrained decoding 作为 training-time format guarantee，模型并未充分学会 JSON format 的内在结构。更关键的是，parseable subset 偏向 easy instances（mean greedy F1 0.68 vs full set 0.644），因为 format-compliant 的 free-form output 更可能出现在模型 \\\"confident\\\" 的 instances 上——这些恰恰是 oracle headroom 更小、selection 价值更低的 instances。\\nSelection F1 几乎不变（NER +0.3pp, p=0.42; RE -0.3pp, p=0.65）直接否定了 bottleneck 假说。 如果 score compression 是 selection 失败的主因，那么恢复 variance 应该恢复 selection——但没有。 这说明 logprob 作为 scalar signal 的排序失败不是因为被压缩，而是因为 IE 的 set-valued output 空间中，generation probability 与 output quality（F1）之间本就不存在强的单调关系。一个 sample 可以有高 logprob（模型 confident）但 F1 低（confident about wrong entities），也可以有低 logprob （探索性 output）但 F1 高（偶然命中更多 gold entities）。\\nRE 更差是因为 free-form 下 relation format 的 parse failure 更高（35%），且 RE 的组合空间 (entity pairs × relation types) 远大于 NER，使得 scalar signal 的信息论上限更低。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ner_llama_conll\",\n    \"description\": \"LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003 进行 NER inference (N=8, T=1.0)。 Cross-model × cross-dataset validation，强化 model-agnostic claim。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"greedy_f1\": 0.918,\n      \"oracle_f1\": 0.945,\n      \"oracle_headroom\": 0.027,\n      \"n_instances\": 3453,\n      \"n_valid\": 2756,\n      \"sj_rho_full\": 0.43,\n      \"fk_rho_full\": 0.42,\n      \"logprob_rho_full\": 0.31,\n      \"em_rho_full\": 0.43,\n      \"voting_conf_rho_full\": 0.42,\n      \"sj_auroc_full\": 0.7,\n      \"logprob_auroc_full\": 0.76,\n      \"logprob_selection_f1\": 0.919,\n      \"sj_selection_f1\": 0.916,\n      \"voting_selection_f1\": 0.917,\n      \"random_selection_f1\": 0.912,\n      \"oracle_f1_selection\": 0.945,\n      \"qwen_conll_sj_rho\": 0.436,\n      \"llama_conll_sj_rho\": 0.43,\n      \"delta_sj_rho\": -0.006\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model QE Comparison on CoNLL-2003\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"Qwen ρ\",\n          \"LLaMA ρ\",\n          \"Δρ\",\n          \"Qwen AUROC\",\n          \"LLaMA AUROC\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SJ\",\n            \"0.436\",\n            \"0.43\",\n            \"−0.006\",\n            \"0.80\",\n            \"0.70\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FK\",\n            \"0.400\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"+0.020\",\n            \"0.77\",\n            \"0.70\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"logprob\",\n            \"0.316\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"−0.006\",\n            \"0.75\",\n            \"0.76\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EM\",\n            \"0.451\",\n            \"0.43\",\n            \"−0.021\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"0.70\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"voting_conf\",\n            \"0.424\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"−0.004\",\n            \"0.79\",\n            \"0.71\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model validation 成功但对 worst 档的核心困境帮助不大。可以作为 Table 1 的一行补充 model-agnostic evidence，但不改变 selection failure 的 narrative。在 worst 档的 paper 中，这个实验从 \\\"strengthening the bottleneck claim\\\" 降级为 \\\"confirming QE generalization\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档对 exp-017 的影响有限——这个实验是 cross-model validation，不直接依赖 bottleneck 假说。 CoNLL-2003 是 \\\"easy\\\" NER dataset（greedy F1 ~0.92），oracle headroom 仅 ~0.027， selection 的理论上限就很低。LLaMA 在 CoNLL 上的表现应与 Qwen 高度一致 （exp_017_llama_conll_infer 已有 SJ ρ=0.431 的数据佐证），因为两个 8B 模型在 well-studied benchmark 上的 behavior 趋同。\\n在 worst 档下，这个实验的结果本身是 \\\"positive\\\"（cross-model consistency confirmed）， 但对论文的帮助有限：它只证明了 QE 信号的 model-agnostic property，而 worst 档的核心问题 是 selection 失败的叙事需要 pivot。Cross-model validation 对 \\\"fundamental hardness\\\" 叙事是中性的——不增强也不削弱。\\nSelection F1 在 CoNLL 上接近 greedy（+0.1pp），与 SciERC 的 pattern 一致。 但因为 headroom 只有 2.7pp，即使 oracle 也只能提升这么多，所以 selection failure 在 CoNLL 上的 diagnostic value 很低。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ner_ood_robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"在 OOD 条件下（cross-domain transfer）测试 NER consistency signal 的鲁棒性。 依赖 exp-003 (WNUT-17) 的 fine-tuned model 做 domain shift 测试。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ood_greedy_f1\": 0.35,\n      \"ood_oracle_f1\": 0.52,\n      \"ood_headroom\": 0.17,\n      \"ood_sj_rho_full\": 0.05,\n      \"ood_fk_rho_full\": 0.08,\n      \"ood_logprob_rho_full\": -0.3,\n      \"ood_voting_conf_rho_full\": 0.09,\n      \"ood_sj_auroc\": 0.53,\n      \"ood_logprob_auroc\": 0.42,\n      \"ood_sample_f1_pct_zero\": 62.0,\n      \"ood_n_instances\": 1287,\n      \"ood_logprob_negative_rho\": true,\n      \"ood_logprob_overconfidence_on_wrong\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: In-domain vs OOD Signal Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"In-domain ρ (SciERC)\",\n          \"OOD ρ\",\n          \"Δρ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SJ\",\n            \"0.36\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"−0.31\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FK\",\n            \"0.27\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"−0.19\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"logprob\",\n            \"0.21\",\n            \"−0.30\",\n            \"−0.51\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"voting_conf\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"0.09\",\n            \"−0.29\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD 实验在 worst 档下提供的额外信息有限——exp-003 WNUT-17 已经展示了同样的 pathology。 且 exp-003 status=orphaned，exp-011 依赖 exp-003，实际执行概率极低。 如果执行，它强化了 \\\"logprob is unreliable under shift\\\" 的 claim，但这不是论文的核心。 建议 worst 档下不投入 GPU hours 在这个实验上，将资源集中于 exp-018 的 robustness checks。\\n\\n\\nOOD 条件下所有信号急剧退化。Greedy F1 降到 ~0.35 意味着模型在目标域基本失效， >60% samples F1=0。在这个 regime 下： (1) SJ/FK/voting 的 ρ 接近 0 因为大部分 instances 的 N 个 samples 全部 F1=0， 无 variance 可供 correlation 捕捉； (2) Logprob 出现 WNUT-17 同样的 pathology：ρ 为负（-0.30），模型对 OOD 输入 过度自信——logprob 高的 samples 反而更差，因为模型 \\\"confidently\\\" 产出 in-domain patterns 而非 target domain 的正确 entities； (3) 这与 exp-003 (WNUT-17 logprob ρ=-0.41) 的发现一致。\\n在 worst 档下，这个实验的解读方向改变：不再是 \\\"OOD shows limitations of consistency signals\\\" （这太 obvious），而是作为 \\\"logprob overconfidence under distribution shift\\\" 的额外证据， 支持 \\\"scalar signals fail for structural reasons, not just compression\\\" 的论点。 但 P2 priority + exp-003 已经 orphaned 意味着这个实验大概率不会执行。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"simple_verifier_baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"训练 supervised verifier（DeBERTa-v3-large 或 Qwen3-8B classification head）在 existing (input, output, F1) 数据上。测试 verifier 能否部分 close selection gap， 为 unsupervised signal 的 failure 提供 upper bound。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"train_n_instances\": 529,\n      \"train_n_samples_per_instance\": 8,\n      \"train_total_pairs\": 4232,\n      \"train_val_split\": \"5-fold CV\",\n      \"deberta_auroc_ner\": 0.72,\n      \"deberta_auroc_re\": 0.66,\n      \"deberta_selection_f1_ner\": 0.652,\n      \"deberta_selection_delta_vs_greedy_ner_pp\": 0.8,\n      \"deberta_selection_p_ner\": 0.18,\n      \"deberta_selection_f1_re\": 0.398,\n      \"deberta_selection_delta_vs_greedy_re_pp\": -0.5,\n      \"deberta_selection_p_re\": 0.55,\n      \"best_unsupervised_auroc_ner\": 0.749,\n      \"deberta_vs_best_unsupervised_auroc_ner\": -0.029,\n      \"best_unsupervised_selection_ner\": 0.65,\n      \"deberta_vs_best_unsupervised_selection_ner\": 0.002,\n      \"oracle_selection_f1_ner\": 0.776,\n      \"oracle_selection_f1_re\": 0.588,\n      \"verifier_headroom_capture_ner_pct\": 6.1,\n      \"verifier_headroom_capture_re_pct\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Supervised Verifier vs Unsupervised Signals\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"NER AUROC\",\n          \"NER Sel. F1\",\n          \"RE AUROC\",\n          \"RE Sel. F1\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DeBERTa verifier (5-fold CV)\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"0.652\",\n            \"0.66\",\n            \"0.398\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EM (best unsupervised AUROC)\",\n            \"0.749\",\n            \"0.650\",\n            \"0.706\",\n            \"0.403\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Logprob (best unsupervised sel.)\",\n            \"0.578\",\n            \"0.650\",\n            \"0.600\",\n            \"0.410\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Greedy baseline\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.644\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.403\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Oracle\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.776\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.588\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-019 在 worst 档下的价值在于 closing the loop：即使 supervised signal 也无法显著 close selection gap，说明问题不在于 signal quality 而在于 task structure。但执行条件 苛刻（需要 exp-018 先完成 + 还有 DDL 前时间），且 4K training data 的 verifier 说服力 有限。建议：如果时间允许，作为 1 天 quick experiment 执行，结果写入 Discussion 而非 main results。如果时间不够，在 paper 中引用 exp-016 ensemble（logistic regression on 5 signals）作为 proxy supervised baseline，其 AUROC 0.735 已经 ≤ best single signal EM 0.749，传达同样的 message。\\n\\nWorst 档下 supervised verifier 也基本失败，原因有三层：\\n(1) 训练数据不足：529 instances × 8 samples = 4232 training pairs，对于 DeBERTa 这种 encoder 来说数据量极少。5-fold CV 下每折只有 ~3400 training pairs，严重 overfit 风险。 即使不 overfit，模型学到的更多是 \\\"哪些 input 难\\\"（instance difficulty）而非 \\\"哪个 output 好\\\"（within-instance quality variation），因为 inter-instance F1 variance 远大于 intra-instance F1 variance。\\n(2) Feature gap：DeBERTa 只能看到 (input, output) text pair，无法 access logprob 或 其他 generation metadata。它本质上在做 NLI-style 判断 \\\"output 是否合理\\\"，而 IE 的 \\\"合理性\\\" 需要 precise span matching，这超出了 encoder 的 zero-shot 能力。即使 fine-tune， 4K pairs 不足以学会 IE-specific quality patterns。\\n(3) IE 的组合复杂性：即使 verifier AUROC 达到 0.72（超过 logprob 的 0.578）， 这仍然是 instance-level discrimination（\\\"这个 instance 的 output 总体好不好\\\"）， 而非 within-instance ranking（\\\"这 8 个 candidate 中哪个最好\\\"）。 AUROC 0.72 不等于 selection 能力——exp-016 已经证明 AUROC 0.749 的 EM 信号 selection 也只有 +0.6pp（n.s.）。\\nVerifier 的 headroom capture rate 极低（NER 6.1%，RE 0%）与 unsupervised signals 的 pattern 一致，说明 selection gap 不是 \\\"signals 太弱\\\" 而是 \\\"task structure 使得 instance-level scoring 根本不够\\\"。这反而支持了 worst 档的核心论点：需要 sub-instance level 的 selection mechanism（如 entity-level MBR），scalar scoring 存在 fundamental ceiling。\\n但 reviewer 价值有限：verifier 没有显著超过 best unsupervised signal， \\\"supervised 也不行\\\" 这个 claim 在 4K training pairs 下 underpowered， reviewer 会 argue \\\"给足够数据 verifier 肯定能 work\\\"。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":391,"startLine":1,"totalLines":391}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01J4H5PQGrx4j6YNHWptVBuf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me understand the key data and framing for the \"worst\" tier paper:\n\n**Core narrative (worst tier)**: The free-form decoding ablation **failed** to confirm the \"constrained decoding bottleneck\" hypothesis. Removing constraints only marginally improved logprob variance (0.03→0.07 median range) and did NOT improve selection F1. This means the paper must pivot to a \"fundamental selection hardness in structured prediction\" universal negative finding, with QE framework as primary contribution.\n\n**Experiments to cover:**\n1. **freeform_decoding_ablation** - The key ablation showing constrained decoding is NOT the bottleneck\n\n\n2. **ner_llama_conll** - Cross-model validation on CoNLL-2003 with LLaMA\n3. **ner_ood_robustness** - OOD robustness test showing signal degradation\n4. **simple_verifier_baseline** - Supervised verifier also fails, confirming fundamental hardness\n\nI'm also pulling the key QE results from the framing document—specifically the NER full dataset correlation of 0.379 for voting confidence—which will anchor the main findings.\n\nNow I'm looking at the performance metrics across different selection methods: logprob achieves 0.650 on selection while oracle reaches 0.776, and for relation extraction the greedy approach gets 0.404 versus oracle's 0.585. The AUROC numbers show EM performing best at 0.749 while logprob lags at 0.578.\n\nI'm structuring the paper around four core points: that scalar signals fundamentally fail at structured IE tasks, positioning the QE framework as the main contribution, showing through ablation that the bottleneck isn't where we thought, and demonstrating that even supervised approaches can't overcome this limitation. Now I'll write this up in EMNLP format.\n\nI'm planning the paper structure with an abstract, introduction, brief related work, then the method section covering the QE framework and selection protocol. The experiments will showcase the main QE results, free-form decoding ablation, cross-model validation, OOD robustness tests, and the supervised verifier baseline, each with supporting tables. Then I'll wrap up with analysis and conclusions.\n\nActually, I need to refocus the narrative here—the paper needs to pivot toward establishing this as a universal negative finding about selection hardness in structured prediction, with the QE framework as the primary contribution rather than just a bottleneck identification story.\n\nThe real insight is that constrained decoding wasn't the bottleneck after all; the gap stems from something more fundamental about IE's combinatorial output space. No scalar signal can reliably select in this setting, which is actually a stronger and more interesting result. The QE framework still has value for quality estimation with decent AUROC around 0.75, just not for selection itself.\n\nNow I'll write the paper in ACL/EMNLP style.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6923,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8028,"cache_read_input_tokens":23171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8028},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14f41098-1a14-4cd2-befd-b73275d72bd6","uuid":"199e6981-ffee-405e-bfa5-a54da0d7de2a"}
